**Standard error of the sample mean (under the null)**  

\[
SE = \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
    = \frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
    \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
    \approx 0.2215
\]

So the standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the sample mean—i.e., the standard error used in the null‑hypothesis test—is **≈ 0.22**.
